  "query_preview": "..\nWhile the upper-level ridge over the area moves to the east\ntonight and Monday, SW flow aloft will keep temperatures above\nnormal through Tuesday. A shortwave trough moves inland Monday and\nTuesday from the Pacific. This wave will move through Montana on\nWednesday. The system will bring rain and snow Tuesday night and\nWednesday with a cold front. \n\nPrecipitation will begin as rain in the west Tuesday evening and\nspread east late Tuesday night and Wednesday morning. Temperatures\nwill cool enough by Wednesday morning for either a rain/snow mix\nor change to all snow mainly in the west. Locations north of US-2\ntowards the international border west of Scobey and higher\nelevations of the Little Rocky Mountains near Zortman may see \nsnow accumulations between 0.5\" and 1\" depending on timing of the \nrain to mixed precipitation and snow transitions and the current\nNBM forecast. EC, GFS, and CMC ensembles have somewhat higher \nsnowfall amounts especially NW of line from Zortman, Malta to \nOpheim so the snow forecast will need to watched in future model\nruns. As the main upper trough settles into the intermountain \nwest Wednesday and Thursday cooling aloft will drive temperatures \ncloser to normal.\n\nLarge scale upper troughing continues across the western US\nthrough the week into next weekend with another distinct upper \nlow moving inland at the end of the work week. This system will \nsee much cooler temperatures, but less moisture. The highest \nprecipitation chances are across southern portions of the \nforecast area. There is a fair amount of uncertainty in the \nquantity and spatial extent of precipitation, however, there is\nmuch higher confidence it will fall as snow rather than rain.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Lowered minimum temperatures through Wednesday. Lowered high\n  temperature Wednesday.\n\n- Confidence in fair conditions persisting through Monday is high. \n\n- Confidence in mid week pattern change is high.\n\n- Confidence in precipitation Tuesday night and Wednesday is\n  moderate. Increasing confidence in a transition to snow late\n  Tuesday night into Wednesday morning.\n\n- Confidence in Tuesday night and Wednesday snow forecast is low.",
